; A `pure` claim over a call the effect walk cannot resolve, in each of
; the four shapes that reach it.
;
; The walk follows call edges and reference sites. A function value that
; travels through MEMORY - into a struct field, into a data constructor,
; into a `let` from either - arrives somewhere with no call edge behind
; it, so the concrete effect set at the call comes back EMPTY. The
; effects land on whoever NAMED the function; nothing carries them
; across the store to the load.
;
; Empty used to be indistinguishable from pure. All three compiled
; clean, ran, and reached `__syscall3`, while `symbols` printed `#pure`
; with no `#effects=` beside it - the analysis asserting exactly what it
; had failed to look at. The sentinel that records an unresolved call
; had been in the source the whole time, skipped by two consumers and
; produced by nobody since f6ddc2e removed its last producer along with
; the completeness gate its own comment describes.
;
; `viaTransparent` is the fourth and it is not a memory read. `h` is a
; PARAMETER, so calling it is modelled - that is what effect
; transparency is for, and `#effect-params=h` says so. What is NOT
; modelled is the value handed INTO the transparent position: `b.f` is
; a word out of a struct, `apply1` calls whatever it is given, and no
; call edge runs from the field store to that call. "Pure modulo its
; function parameters" excuses `h`; it does not excuse an argument the
; walk cannot name.
;
; A fifth shape is marked in `typecheck.ax` and is NOT tested here
; because it cannot be written: a lambda's own parameter is opaque for
; the same reason, but a called lambda parameter does not type-check
; (`AX3004`, `expected function type, found _tN` - inference never gives
; a lambda parameter a function type), so no well-typed program reaches
; it. The marker is set anyway, because `-1` there would CLAIM the
; binder was attributed somewhere, and it is not.
(:: doIO (-> Int Int))

(fn (doIO n) (__syscall3 1 1 n 0))

(struct Box
  (f : (-> Int Int)))

(data Holder
  (Wrap (-> Int Int)))

(:: install Box)

(fn (install) (Box doIO))

(:: hold Holder)

(fn (hold) (Wrap doIO))

;@axiom:pure
(:: viaField (-> Box Int))

(fn (viaField b) (b.f 7))

;@axiom:pure
(:: viaLet (-> Box Int))

(fn (viaLet b)
  (let ((g b.f))
    (g 7)
  )
)

;@axiom:pure
(:: viaPattern (-> Holder Int))

(fn (viaPattern h)
  (match h
    ((Wrap f) (f 7))
  )
)

(:: apply1 (-> (-> Int Int) Int))

(fn (apply1 g) (g 1))

;@axiom:pure
(:: viaTransparent (-> (-> (-> Int Int) Int) Box Int))

(fn (viaTransparent h b) (h b.f))

(:: main Int)

(fn (main) (+ (+ (viaField install) (viaLet install)) (+ (viaPattern hold) (viaTransparent apply1 install))))
